  "example_scope": "A directly runnable scalar/atomic Rust host imports only std and the public leselang_vm::native facade. Original parsing, catalog compilation, pure computation, helper expansion, capture and LocalVm reentry execute the program; adapter trait implementations own native metadata, policy and effects, not a replacement evaluator. No test source is included and no product service, account, SQLite, GUI toolkit, worker or storage backend is needed.",
  "authority_scope": "Compilation validates current catalog capabilities and cold source. Dispatch checks the live local lease, exact identity serial, current capability, original schema pointer and next unsettled call before bounded checked native mutation. Cancellation stops before a second dispatch; late authority revocation fails after the first completed effect. These private in-process identities are not an external receipt authentication or durable replay protocol.",
  "failure_scope": "The example classifies native failure through with_host_outcome, explicitly accepts successful replies and polls for continuation. Failure output preserves partial counter state, successful call count and available remaining fuel, never claiming rollback. Six example tests cover normal source/capture/reentry, cancellation, initial/late authority refusal, native failure without committing the rejected call, all smaller completion budgets and cold invalid/oversized sources.",
